#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672347 :multistep/context "Source question: Problem 3(a)–(b), PDF page 4.\n\nLet $R$ be any region in the plane not containing the origin. The source’s requested assertions are preserved below." :multistep/id #uuid "c6e7d018-3e8a-587d-afcd-7a773fd01437" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672210 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672324}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672301 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672424}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672349 :multistep/context "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 8](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/8).\n\nA Bernoulli equation has the form $y\\prime+P(x)y=Q(x)y^n$. It is linear when n=0 or n=1. Otherwise, the substitution $u=y^{1-n}$ gives $u\\prime+(1-n)P(x)u=(1-n)Q(x)$.\n\nConsider $xy\\prime+y=-9xy^2$, y(1)=2." :multistep/id #uuid "c8381da5-8217-5e2f-951a-5a8d56f87e63" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672056 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672160}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672107 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672211}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672176 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672417}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672312 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672236}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672429 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672181}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672367 :multistep/context "Source question: Problem 4(a)–(c), PDF page 5.\n\nEvaluate each integral using your method of choice. Show your supporting work." :multistep/id #uuid "d4bd02a6-c6e1-5cd4-9064-5869312fd8b8" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672179 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672117}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672214 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672129}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672404 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672305}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672383 :multistep/context "Source question: Assignment item (4), textbook Exercise **2.1.60**, parts (a)–(b), [printed page 98 (PDF page 110)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=110).\n\nA single row operation applied to\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1\\\\0&5&1\\\\2&-1&4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1\\\\2&4&5\\\\2&-1&4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "de690609-e409-598e-bce6-b2b78483774f" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672219 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672115}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672415 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672138}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672407 :multistep/context "Source question: Assignment item (3), textbook Exercise **2.1.58**, parts (a)–(b), [printed page 98 (PDF page 110)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=110).\n\nA single row operation applied to\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1\\\\0&5&1\\\\2&-1&4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1\\\\0&10&2\\\\2&-1&4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "f19741ef-94eb-57eb-863f-b16abc4d342e" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672061}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672423 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672084}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672416 :multistep/context "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 5](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/5).\n\nThe Gompertz model for a limited population is $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}=c\\ln(K/P)P$, where c is constant and K is the carrying capacity. Use c=0.2, K=3000, and P(0)=500." :multistep/id #uuid "f67e8290-3023-5275-8946-3b9eff4422a1" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672266 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672281}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672357 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672348}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674418 :multistep/context "Consider the function $f(x)=6\\sin\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)$. Use this definition throughout the following parts." :multistep/id #uuid "dacd92e7-7677-5287-bce3-b13ef2e494d6" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674421 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233414}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674422 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233415}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674423 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233416}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674424 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233417}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674425 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233418}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674426 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233419}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674427 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233420}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674428 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233421}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674429 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233422}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674430 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233423}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674432 :multistep/context "A particle has velocity $v(t)=4\\csc^2 t$, measured in meters per second. Use this function for the first four parts. The second particle is introduced in part 5." :multistep/id #uuid "fee0cb2f-832e-59ea-b2aa-52e2d78c1aea" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674435 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233489}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674436 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233492}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674437 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233486}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674438 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233488}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674439 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233490}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674440 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233491}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674441 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233487}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674443 :multistep/context "A bakery models its weekly profit in dollars by $p(x)=ax^2+bx$, where $x$ is the number of cakes sold in a week and $a$ and $b$ are constants. Use the information 